@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Research
+
+## Request flows examined
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java`
+  maps `POST /api/v1/cart` and `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}` directly to the legacy shopping-cart facade. These methods do not inspect the request principal, so carts created or modified with a customer token keep a null `customerId`.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`
+  has customer-aware `addToCart(Customer, ...)`, but the API does not call it. Its generic cart creation path creates a cart without a customer. The existing customer-cart facade delegates to `ShoppingCartService.getShoppingCart`.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`
+  filters a customer's carts to uncompleted carts but returns `validCart.get(0)`, with no ordering. This does not implement “most recently created or changed”; cart reads also do not record a change timestamp.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartRepository.java`
+  exposes `findByCustomer` without store filtering or ordering. Store isolation and deterministic current-cart selection therefore need to be enforced in the service/repository query.
+
+## Totals and checkout
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderTotalApi.java`
+  authenticates with `customerService.getByNick`, loads the cart by id, and checks ownership. It calls `response.sendError(503, ...)` when the customer lookup fails and catches every exception, including errors caused by the normal response flow, then emits 503. The total calculation itself calls `OrderService.caculateOrderTotal(..., customer, ...)`, which is the same customer/address-aware calculation used by checkout.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+  authenticated checkout loads any cart by code and does not verify that its `customerId` belongs to the authenticated customer. It catches all exceptions and converts them to 503. `OrderFacadeImpl.processOrder` recalculates the total using the customer and throws `com.salesmanager.core.business.exception.ConversionException` with the calculated amount when `Payment.amount` differs; guest checkout lets that validation error reach the normal 400 handling, while authenticated checkout hides it as 503.
+- Successful checkout calls `ShoppingCartFacade.setOrderId`, so the cart becomes ineligible for the current-cart lookup once the order is persisted. Ownership must be checked before processing so another customer's cart cannot be ordered.
+
+## Customer orders
+
+- `GET /api/v1/auth/orders` in `OrderApi` passes `page` directly as `start` to `OrderFacadeImpl.getReadableOrderList(store, customer, ...)`.
+- That facade builds an `OrderCriteria` and calls the deprecated `OrderRepositoryImpl.listByStore`. The query orders by `o.id desc` and filters `o.customerId`, so the order identity/filter and newest-first behavior are present, but `listByStore` only sets `totalCount`; it never sets `totalPages`.
+- `OrderFacadeImpl` returns `recordsTotal` from `totalCount`, but the empty/non-empty customer-list path does not reliably set `totalPages`, and the API’s `page`/`count` contract needs page-based pagination rather than treating `page` as a row offset. `ReadableList` exposes the required `recordsTotal` and `totalPages` fields.
+
+## Files likely affected and related behavior
+
+- Cart ownership/current-cart behavior: shopping-cart API, shopping-cart facade, service/repository query/model timestamp support.
+- Secure cart totals and checkout status/error behavior: `OrderTotalApi`, `OrderApi`.
+- Customer order counts/pages: `OrderFacadeImpl` and/or order repository pagination, while preserving the existing customer-id filter and descending id ordering.
+- Existing guest cart, guest checkout, admin/private order listing, shipping quote calculation, and checkout cart completion must remain unchanged.
+
+## Test/build observations
+
+No source files were edited before this research note. The repository is a multi-module Maven project; targeted tests and a Maven build will be run after implementation.
